00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.589 align:start position:0%
 
what's going on guys this is rob and  welcome back to geek culture explained  meet steve the plant he's going to be  joining us here for a little while and  rumors abound that henry cavill is  joining the mcu that supposedly marvel  studios is courting this guy in order to  give him some unspecified role so let's  start with the cameo type character this  is a guy by the name of zoran although  those of you guys who are familiar with  marvel comics may know him as sun god  now if you're not familiar with this guy  he's actually a really really cool  character so the way this played out is  during jonathan hickman's avengers new  avengers which i absolutely love  basically you had the illuminati you had  the incursions worlds colliding  different things like that and so what  the illuminati had done is they had  formed something called the bridge in  order to figure out how other universes  were faring against the incursions in  one particular universe they had  actually defeated or fended off an  incursion successfully without using any  kind of crazy devices or anything like  that or at least that seemed to be the  case this led to the illuminati  investigating and coming across what was  called the great society and what you  ended up learning here is that on earth  in this alternate reality you had a  group called the archetypes of justice  which was basically a coming together of  the different superheroes that you're  the most familiar with wolverine and  different characters like that albeit  just kind of a different name but they  tried to defend the earth against the  cree and the scrolls and they were  ultimately killed and so what this did  is it led to zoran and what was  essentially the squadron supreme albeit  by a different name banding together and  then defeating the cree and the scrolls  and then once the incursion started  successfully fending off an incursion  which was a pretty big deal now we ended  up learning later on that they use what  was called the the prisms of forever  glass basically it was their universe's  version of the infinity gauntlet which  of course in every reality whenever an  incursion started and anybody tried to  use the infinity gauntlet in their  universe to defeat that incursion the  infinity stones were destroyed in some  capacity it was basically marvel's way  of getting rid of the infinity gauntlet  as a macguffin to essentially save the  day and so what ended up happening is  when the illuminati showed up here they  fought off fought against the great  society and ultimately they ended up  winning when dr strange summoned this  just eldritch demon from another  dimension this led to basically the  death of the great society and then of  course they ended up detonating an  anti-matter bomb blew up the world and  then left but if we move away from sun  god basically being a cameo character  that uh that henry cavill could play in  the mcu we move into a character that he  could play for the long term which i've  been advocating for quite some time and  that is marcus milton of earth 13034  also known as hyperion now hyperion is  the closest you get to a consistently  appearing character in marvel comics  that's their version of superman  technically they have a few characters  like that right you have hyperion you've  got the century robert reynolds you've  also got adam brashear the blue marvel  but hyperion is pretty much the closest  and the reason why is because even his  origin story at least that version of  marcus milton because there's been  different versions of hyperion that have  appeared over the years in marvel the  origin story of that version of hyperion  was almost identical to superman's that  he came from a world which was home to  eternals in an alternate reality and  that when his world and that alternate  reality was basically destroyed he was  sent to that alternate reality's earth  he landed there and he was taught or at  least raised by a guy named father who  taught him like a moral compass what it  meant to be a good guy different things  like that that story directly mirrors  superman right the explosion of krypton  being sent to earth raised by jonathan  and martha kent and taught what it means  to be a human being that just screws up  all the time and so what ended up  happening here is that hyperion was  basically the last survivor really the  last survivor of the universe when an  incursion started and there was a point  in this comment to show you how powerful  this guy was there was a point in the  story when he held two universes apart  it was only for a few moments but he had  enough power to hold universes apart  from each other now ultimately those  universes collided but he still couldn't  be destroyed and in fact he just sat in  this giant white vacant space that used  to be his universe ultimately he was  pulled out of that space by a group  called advanced idea mechanics and then  he was brought to the main marvel  universe ultimately rescued by the  avengers and then joined the team now  the reason why these two characters are  the most viable options for henry cavill  to play even though there's hundreds if  not thousands of possibilities for  characters that they simply haven't  introduced yet the reason why this is  the most viable is twofold the first is  because it's just a great way for marvel  studios to have henry cavill continue to  play a superman type character and just  kind of jab at warner brothers and just  be like we can make a superman better  than you can but the other reason and  really the most serious reason if we're  kind of getting down to business here is  that the stage has been set for this the  stage has been set for both of these  guys to appear in some form or fashion  the incursions are already a thing  that's going on right we know that  that's already taking place across the  multiverse we know the illuminati have  their explanation for why the incursions  are happening but we don't even know if  the illuminati are right about their  estimation for why the incursions are  happening this exact same scenario  unfolded in hickman's avengers new  avengers everybody thought they knew  what was going on until it turned out  they didn't then you learned about the  ivory kings right the white lords of  wild space basically the beyonders who  were the ones that were behind it all or  at least partly the other part was dr  doom which was amazing  but the big thing here is that if we  want to invoke the incursions which we  are already aware of you can literally  just do the story of marcus milton from  earth13034  as a part of an existing movie possibly  its own film and then have him rolled  into the mcu and he becomes part of  whatever the avengers roster is going to  be that goes into kane dynasty and  secret wars and he's now a part of the  multiversal team you could also do the  same thing with sun god right just say  that like instead of getting a whole  great big huge origin story he's just a  superhero that fights alongside another  team that exists on earth in an  alternate reality and that's basically  all you get another reason why the stage  is set for this is because marvel  studios is looking for what is in effect  the roster for the next avengers team  some of the characters we've already  seen some of them have been teased like  she-hulk i don't know that she's  actually going to be a long-standing  member of the reality i think here is  that while the show is interesting  reception to her character is lukewarm  at best so i don't know if people are  really chomping at the bit and are  excited at the idea that like she-hulk's  gonna become part of the avengers i'm  sure somebody is but the thing about  this is that it allows the mcu to expand  on their existing roster and take  characters that we're already the most  familiar with the incredible hulk thor  different characters like that and add  someone to them or potentially replace  that character with someone like henry  cavill because the reality here is i  just don't see henry cavill as being a  temporary character i don't see him  being a short-term guy i see him being a  long-term guy so having said that uh let  me know what you guys think down in the  comments section let me know what you  think this role will be for henry cavill  do you think it'll be either one of  these do you have your own guesses on  who you think henry cavill is going to  play and if you do make sure you post  those below thank you all for watching  and i will catch you all later  peace

